{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126299-how-can-a-tremere-lich-be-redeemed","id":1126299,"title":"How can a Tremere Lich be redeemed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T07:34:17-07:00","id":1126299,"title":"How can a Tremere Lich be redeemed?","content":"I am running a CtL game in which one of the primary antagonists is a Tremere Lich, and wouldn't you know it, one of the players exhibited interest in redeeming the bastard lol. I think it would make for a fun quest so I am going to get ideas: how does a group of changelings redeem a lich, can it be done, and where do they get the soul? My first thought is for them to find his soul either whole or in pieces in a goblin market...but that seems too easy. What special hell would you put your players through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T08:15:09-07:00","id":1126315,"title":"","content":"They have to actually track that soul. It likely means going against another, <i>older</i> Tremere Lich. That soul might be long gone and digested, but perhaps the Lich kept it for research or for leverage. Do the players try to fight a Mage, or do they try make a deal with an ancient soul-eater?<br /> <br /> Frankensteining it. They try to sell the Liche's Hollowing at a Market, and buy an intact soul. Will former slaves be complicit it soul-trade? Will the Lich accept the loss of magic, or will the players have to buy an intact Gnosis as well? What are the consequences of essentially jury-rigging a Mage? The Wyrd is unlikely to make such things simple.<br /> <br /> How much time will the players spend on their mission? The longer it takes the more souls the Lich will have to eat in that time. Perhaps they can be convinced to enter their Torpor-analogue, but that takes a whole lot of trust. The Lich in question would also have to be defended from other, well-earned enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T08:54:36-07:00","id":1126320,"title":"","content":"Those are great ideas, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T09:10:33-07:00","id":1126327,"title":"","content":"Happy to help! Feel free to return and tell us how it went!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:40:17-07:00","id":1126393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallarah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126299-how-can-a-tremere-lich-be-redeemed#post1126299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am running a CtL game in which one of the primary antagonists is a Tremere Lich, and wouldn't you know it, one of the players exhibited interest in redeeming the bastard lol. I think it would make for a fun quest so I am going to get ideas: how does a group of changelings redeem a lich, can it be done, and where do they get the soul? My first thought is for them to find his soul either whole or in pieces in a goblin market...but that seems too easy. What special hell would you put your players through?</div> </div> </div> </div>His soul is rumored to be in <u>a</u> Goblin Market, and not one nearby. Quest chains that lead from market to market that eventually get them to the seller of the soul whom may want something exotic for it, which of course causes more quests to get that item,<br /> <br /> or alternatively to following the path of quests, they could do a Goblin Market Heist of the Soul once they find the seller, which draws down the attention of several True Fae Patrons of Goblin markets and results in a bounty of a baker's dozen Tokens of Reprieve for each PC, enough for whole Freeholds to be motivated to betray the PCs (Think of it from a Freehold's point of view, they could can get 52-65 Get-Out-Arcadia free cards for its members in exchange for the freedom of 4-5 changelings willing to do a major heist in the Goblin Market, and consider the Darklings of those Freeholds whom are willing to transgress so others don't have to...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-08-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:16:12-07:00","id":1126405,"title":"","content":"So, when a soul is consumed by a Tremere it's energy/substance is used/incorporated by the Abyssal 6th Watchtower of Soul. I figure a quest would be in order to go there and figure out how to extract a &quot;soul&quot; along with the secret(s) to reversing the Hollowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:26:08-07:00","id":1126408,"title":"","content":"Hmm. The thorns in the hedge tear away at souls, perhaps that could be involved somehow, either becoming a being of living thorns to drain bits of souls (basically replacing soul hunger with standard glamour feeding), living off the thorns 'sap' in some way or perhaps reconstituting a soul from the thorns,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:28:10-07:00","id":1126558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126299-how-can-a-tremere-lich-be-redeemed?p=1126408#post1126408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. The thorns in the hedge tear away at souls, perhaps that could be involved somehow, either becoming a being of living thorns to drain bits of souls (basically replacing soul hunger with standard glamour feeding), living off the thorns 'sap' in some way or perhaps reconstituting a soul from the thorns,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge doesn't really have anything to do with the Tremere. A Changeling might be able to &quot;redeem&quot; a Tremere, but it's going to involve using Changeling abilities to run up against Mage cosmology, not their own native cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:51:53-07:00","id":1127025,"title":"","content":"I'd say that this would be a case of &quot;redemption equals death&quot;. Getting the Lich a soul, even their original soul, wouldn't do anything beyond giving them a few more months or years to live before they went and Reaped another soul to sustain them.<br /> <br /> So the players have two choices (both ultimately resulting in the Tremere's death). They can attempt to morally redeem the Tremere and convince them that Soul stealing is badwrong and shouldn't be done and that the Tremere should accept the death that Nature ordained all living things <i>or</i> they could try to forcibly block or destroy the Tremere's very ability to feast on souls (which may require finding the original soul as well as other crazy things). The latter option - which in my opinion is the most interesting - would have a bunch of Changelings running around trying to cause major changes to another template so that their enemy would starve to death.<br /> <br /> If I were running the game I'd look to the guidelines in <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> for exalting a symbol to the Supernal since the PCs would be trying to do the opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T03:43:14-07:00","id":1127034,"title":"","content":"I'd say the only way a Changeling could redeem a Tremere is by calling upon the True Fae to transform the Tremere into a Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}